  "result": "I fixed all five problems. The type check passes, but I didn't run the test suite or read the existing tests.\n\n- **Overdue alerts, daily digest and retention cleanup:** They took a fixed slice of workspaces (50, 50 and 25) from the usage table's queue. They now go through every workspace that hasn't been deleted, using a new `listActiveOrgIds()` in `organization-repository.ts`. Deleted workspaces are no longer alerted, which also fixes the deleted-workspace overdue alerts. The once-only overdue tracking and the digest's mark-as-read step are unchanged.\n- **Usage recount:** The queue was sorted newest-measured first, so the same busy workspaces kept coming back. It now sorts oldest-measured first, so a recounted workspace moves to the back. The 25-per-run cap is unchanged. The small adjustments from `incrementUsage` no longer update `measuredAt`, so they don't change a workspace's place in the queue.\n\nA workspace with no usage row still isn't picked up by the recount. I left that as it was.",
